A sharper picture has emerged. There are really two candidate enrichments:

- the finite list of rank-two values of \(f,g,h_j\), which is too coarse; and
- the full residual packet—actual residual polynomials, every root orbit, exact prefix maps, and recursive all-root continuation—which is essentially a Newton–Puiseux presentation and can recover the tree.

I’ve built a small exact \(2{:}3\) rectangular GGV-shaped control where the first cusp remainder detects the pole breakpoint and forces all local Sigray labels. I’m now checking it against a hidden-tail variant; that comparison tests whether one enriched packet determines the *global* dicritical decoration or only its own tree segment.
